From: XP Explorer
Subject: [PATCH] server: keep the DACL of files for XP's shell too

Purpose: stop XP's shell32 from asking "The Recycle Bin on C:\ is corrupted.
Do you want to empty the Recycle Bin for this drive?" the first time it opens
a drive's RECYCLER folder (a search in Local Hard Drives, for example).
Windows XP behavior: shell32 creates RECYCLER\<user SID> with a DACL made by
GetShellSecurityDescriptor (full access for the user, SYSTEM and
Administrators, each with an inherit-only ACE), and before using it reads the
folder's security (GetFileSecurityW) and compares the DACL byte for byte with
that one. On a mismatch it offers to empty the Recycle Bin.
Wine before: patch 0120 keeps a file's DACL in the user.wine.dacl extended
attribute only in the Windows 7 shell session; elsewhere the DACL is made from
the Unix mode, so XP's comparison always failed.
Change: keep and return the stored DACL in XP's shell session too
(WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL without WIN4WINE_SHELL), as patch 0120 does for
WIN4WINE_SHELL=win7. Folders made before this keep failing the comparison;
xp-explorer/scripts/prefix.py gives them XP's DACL when the session starts.
Evidence: with XP's session, a new C:\RECYCLER\S-1-5-21-0-0-0-1000 carries the
six ACEs and a search for "win" in Local Hard Drives no longer asks.
Scope: only with WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL and no WIN4WINE_SHELL, or
WIN4WINE_SHELL=win7; ReactOS's session behaves as before.
---
 server/fd.c | 12 ++++++------
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

--- a/server/fd.c
+++ b/server/fd.c
@@ -2467,10 +2467,10 @@
 
 #define XATTR_DACL XATTR_USER_PREFIX "wine.dacl"
 
-/* With the Windows 7 shell (WIN4WINE_SHELL=win7, with the WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL
- * opt-in), the DACL given to a file or directory is kept in an extended attribute
- * and returned instead of the one made from the Unix mode: Windows 7's shell checks
- * the DACL of the folders it creates, such as the recycle bin. */
+/* With the XP or Windows 7 shell (no WIN4WINE_SHELL, or WIN4WINE_SHELL=win7, with
+ * the WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL opt-in), the DACL given to a file or directory is kept
+ * in an extended attribute and returned instead of the one made from the Unix mode:
+ * both shells check the DACL of the folders they create, such as the recycle bin. */
 static int stored_dacl_enabled(void)
 {
     static int enabled = -1;
@@ -2478,7 +2478,7 @@
     if (enabled == -1)
     {
         const char *shell = getenv( "WIN4WINE_SHELL" );
-        enabled = getenv( "WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL" ) && shell && !strcasecmp( shell, "win7" );
+        enabled = getenv( "WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL" ) && (!shell || !strcasecmp( shell, "win7" ));
     }
     return enabled;
 }
